    "created_at": "2016-05-17T02:58:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-17T02:58:19Z",
    "body": "This LGTM, although I have a doubts about this part of the spec.\n\nFor example, the note is right but doesn't mention that the item being popped may be an element if the author correctly calls super, but then [HTMLElement constructor](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#htmlelement) step 7 throws an exception doing _element_.[[SetPrototypeOf]](_prototype_). But I am unsure when that could happen in practice, given step 2. (And it seems like calling super multiple times is OK in that case? How would an author write that?)\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/219607277/reactions",
