    "updated_at": "2016-05-17T15:57:30Z",
    "body": "Oh, wow, so you're right that it's impossible to author a class that calls super() multiple times. The second super() call will error before ever calling the constructor.\n\nHowever, it's still possible to trigger that error case. I've added an example to the spec of how to do it.\n\nIn general I want to make these crazy edge cases as clear as possible for implementers in the spec. Would love your thoughts on the new patch which tries to do that. (I added the fact that exceptions thrown in HTMLElement() will impact the stack, as you said.)\n\nI wonder if we should throw in \"upgrade an element\" step 4, if the last entry in the stack is not an already-constructed marker? It seems like the only way that could be possible is if something horrible went wrong, and failing might be better.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
