    "created_at": "2016-05-27T19:05:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-27T19:05:39Z",
    "body": "In particular, this would mean that cases like\n\n``` html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<x-tag></x-tag>\n\n<script>\ncustomElements.define(\"x-tag\", class XTag extends HTMLElement {\n    constructor() {\n        super();\n        try {\n            super();\n        } catch (e) {\n            // purposefully swallow exception so it doesn't reach \"upgrade an element\" step 5\n        }\n    }\n});\n</script>\n```\n\nwould terminate the \"upgrade an element\" algorithm after step 4, instead of moving on and setting the state to `\"custom\"` and calling the custom element callbacks.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
